    "post_rendered": "<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"12\" > is a point in triangle <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" >.</span> We draw perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"12\" > to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e6f986f83255f04596f3cee8797d46f3c40177a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC,AC,AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" > which intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e6f986f83255f04596f3cee8797d46f3c40177a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC,AC,AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" > at <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f824a9531baee67264152c1e8c4d1761a69d842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{1},B_{1},C_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" >.</span> Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"12\" > is circumcenter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > iff perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > is not less than perimeter of triangles <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a163ec90daf5107a462c48dc1e9038d41aea8b91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB_{1}C_{1},BC_{1}A_{1},CB_{1}A_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"182\" height=\"16\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "$O$ is a point in triangle $ABC$. We draw perpendicular from $O$ to $BC,AC,AB$ which intersect $BC,AC,AB$ at $A_{1},B_{1},C_{1}$. Prove that $O$ is circumcenter of triangle $ABC$ iff perimeter of $ABC$ is not less than perimeter of triangles $AB_{1}C_{1},BC_{1}A_{1},CB_{1}A_{1}$.",
